{"id": "en_tornado_home_p2", "total": 70.73, "segments": [{"text": "Part two. A shattered basement window blows flying glass and roaring wind into Sam's safe shelter room.", "start": 0.0, "end": 5.64}, {"text": "He acts fast to escape the dangerous broken glass blowing straight toward his exposed upper body.", "start": 6.04, "end": 9.88}, {"text": "One. Go to the basement, or an interior room on the lowest floor with no windows.", "start": 9.831, "end": 14.0}, {"text": "Sam moves quickly into a small interior closet located far away from any exterior glass windows.", "start": 14.78, "end": 19.08}, {"text": "He steps inside the sturdy building frame to stay safe while heavy structural walls protect him.", "start": 19.52, "end": 23.28}, {"text": "Two. Put as many walls as possible between your body and the severe storm outside.", "start": 23.251, "end": 27.7}, {"text": "He pulls the door shut and positions himself between 3 thick interior walls for safety.", "start": 27.7, "end": 31.98}, {"text": "Three. Cover your head and neck with your arms, a mattress or strong protective helmets.", "start": 31.71, "end": 36.1}, {"text": "Sam stays low and tightly covers his head and neck with his arms and hands.", "start": 36.82, "end": 39.76}, {"text": "Remember that mobile homes and cars are not safe, so seeking sturdy shelter remains vital.", "start": 40.18, "end": 43.84}, {"text": "Outside, violent tornadic wind tears through outer walls while Sam waits in total darkness inside.", "start": 44.54, "end": 49.16}, {"text": "The powerful tornado gradually moves away after 5 intense minutes of crushing structural damage above.", "start": 49.66, "end": 54.02}, {"text": "Sam survives without a single injury because he stayed calm inside a windowless interior room.", "start": 54.02, "end": 58.78}, {"text": "When extreme weather strikes your home, always seek interior protection on the lowest floor level.", "start": 59.16, "end": 63.04}, {"text": "Always head to an interior windowless room during a tornado. Follow for a new scenario tomorrow.", "start": 63.68, "end": 67.58}], "words": [["Part", 0.0, 0.46], ["two.", 0.243, 0.487], ["A", 1.2, 1.3], ["shattered", 1.3, 1.56], ["basement", 1.56, 1.94], ["window", 1.94, 2.28], ["blows", 2.28, 2.46], ["flying", 2.46, 2.94], ["glass", 2.94, 3.2], ["and", 3.2, 3.44], ["roaring", 3.44, 3.78], ["wind", 3.78, 4.2], ["into", 4.2, 4.44], ["Sam's", 4.44, 4.92], ["safe", 4.92, 5.06], ["shelter", 5.06, 5.4], ["room.", 5.4, 5.64], ["He", 6.04, 6.26], ["acts", 6.26, 6.44], ["fast", 6.44, 6.66], ["to", 6.66, 6.86], ["escape", 6.86, 7.08], ["the", 7.08, 7.22], ["dangerous", 7.22, 7.5], ["broken", 7.5, 7.82], ["glass", 7.82, 8.08], ["blowing", 8.08, 8.34], ["straight", 8.34, 8.7], ["toward", 8.7, 8.96], ["his", 8.96, 9.12], ["exposed", 9.12, 9.38], ["upper", 9.38, 9.6], ["body.", 9.6, 9.88], ["One.", 9.831, 10.074], ["Go", 11.12, 11.24], ["to", 11.24, 11.32], ["the", 11.32, 11.4], ["basement,", 11.4, 11.64], ["or", 11.64, 11.86], ["an", 11.86, 11.98], ["interior", 11.98, 12.34], ["room", 12.34, 12.7], ["on", 12.7, 12.82], ["the", 12.82, 12.92], ["lowest", 12.92, 13.12], ["floor", 13.12, 13.42], ["with", 13.42, 13.6], ["no", 13.6, 13.76], ["windows.", 13.76, 14.0], ["Sam", 14.78, 15.08], ["moves", 15.08, 15.26], ["quickly", 15.26, 15.5], ["into", 15.5, 15.76], ["a", 15.76, 15.84], ["small", 15.84, 16.08], ["interior", 16.08, 16.52], ["closet", 16.52, 16.9], ["located", 16.9, 17.24], ["far", 17.24, 17.6], ["away", 17.6, 17.8], ["from", 17.8, 17.96], ["any", 17.96, 18.14], ["exterior", 18.14, 18.48], ["glass", 18.48, 18.78], ["windows.", 18.78, 19.08], ["He", 19.52, 19.68], ["steps", 19.68, 19.82], ["inside", 19.82, 20.24], ["the", 20.24, 20.4], ["sturdy", 20.4, 20.56], ["building", 20.56, 20.86], ["frame", 20.86, 21.1], ["to", 21.1, 21.2], ["stay", 21.2, 21.36], ["safe", 21.36, 21.74], ["while", 21.74, 21.86], ["heavy", 21.86, 22.14], ["structural", 22.14, 22.56], ["walls", 22.56, 22.78], ["protect", 22.78, 23.08], ["h